  "operative_text": "Section 1 (Md. Code Ann., Election Law § 16–904): EXCEPT AS PROVIDED IN SUBSECTION (C) OF THIS SECTION AND § 16–903 OF THIS SUBTITLE, A PERSON MAY NOT: (1) CARRY OR DISPLAY A FIREARM ON THE PREMISES OF A PRIVATELY OR PUBLICLY OWNED BUILDING BEING USED AS A POLLING SITE DURING AN ELECTION, INCLUDING IN A PARKING LOT; OR (2) CARRY OR POSSESS A FIREARM WITHIN 100 FEET OF A POLLING SITE DURING AN ELECTION. A PERSON WHO VIOLATES THIS SECTION IS SUBJECT TO THE CIVIL PENALTY SPECIFIED UNDER § 16–1002 OF THIS TITLE.\nSection 1 (Md. Code Ann., Election Law § 16–904(C)): AN INDIVIDUAL IS NOT IN VIOLATION OF SUBSECTION (B) OF THIS SECTION IF THE INDIVIDUAL IS: (I) A LAW ENFORCEMENT OFFICER IN THE REGULAR COURSE OF THE OFFICER’S DUTY; OR (II) AN OFF–DUTY LAW ENFORCEMENT OFFICER, IF: 1. THE OFFICER IS DISPLAYING THE OFFICER’S BADGE OR CREDENTIAL; AND 2. THE WEAPON CARRIED OR POSSESSED BY THE OFFICER IS CONCEALED."
